  "question": {
    "text": "A solution containing <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>62</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> ethylene glycol in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>250</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> water is cooled to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> . If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub></math> for water is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1.86</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>kg</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> , the amount of water (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> ) separated as ice is:",
